      "snippet": {
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-04T08:00:03Z",
        "channelId": "UC7AWNWptGGpybSgZbV34yBw",
        "title": "The Secret to a Sustainable Health Journey",
        "description": "This week’s conversation with Julie Rice is about the ways building community can help sustain a healthy life — not a goal weight, but a life. After turning SoulCycle into a cultural phenomenon, Julie co-founded Peoplehood around the idea that human connection is a profound practice; it’s also at the forefront of how she is reshaping the Weight Watchers experience. Julie opens up about her own health and career trajectory, her changing relationship to her body, and why connection should be at the heart of wellness conversations.\n\n0:00 Introduction\n0:56 Julie’s Body Journey\n3:21 Finding Weight Watchers\n6:57 Why Community Matters\n10:59 Creating SoulCycle\n14:43 More Than Fitness\n16:32 Weight Loss Unlocks More\n19:47 Joining Weight Watchers\n22:58 Julie’s GLP-1 Journey\n26:00 Rethinking Weight and Biology\n29:14 Weight Watchers Today\n31:43 Reinventing Weight Watchers Workshops\n36:09 The Challenge of Maintenance\n38:56 GLP-1 Mental Health Benefits\n43:15 Building Long-Term Health\n\nGuest: Julie Rice.\n\nThe Weigh In is a Weight Watchers podcast and is not intended as medical advice. Talk to your doctor.\n\nProduced by @DearMediaStudio",
