    {
      "kind": "youtube#playlistItem",
      "etag": "bDoTIpVfaqC5k4hASShGH8n-WZs",
      "id": "VVU3QVdOV3B0R0dweWJTZ1piVjM0eUJ3LklPSUdUYnFFYUpR",
      "snippet": {
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-28T12:24:33Z",
        "channelId": "UC7AWNWptGGpybSgZbV34yBw",
        "title": "Dressing a Changing Body",
        "description": "Nobody talks about how emotionally weird it is to dress a body that's changing. The closet purges. The grief of giving away clothes you loved. The dressing room moments that catch you off guard. Whether to dress the body you have or the one you imagine is in your future. In this episode, Samhita Mukhopadhyay talks with celebrity stylist, creative director, and author Erin Walsh about style as identity when your identity is in flux, and the psychology of body image underneath it all.\n\nGuest: Erin Walsh\n\n0:00 Introduction\n0:55 Meet Erin Walsh\n1:12 Fashion as Transformation\n3:58 Dressing With Intention\n6:23 Using Fashion as Armor\n7:38 Clothes, Weight, and Emotion\n9:14 Identity Inside Your Closet\n10:35 Why Size Inclusivity Matters\n13:05 Embodying Your Best Self\n15:02 Letting Go of Old Clothes\n17:29 Editing Your Closet\n19:48 Dressing Through Body Scrutiny\n23:17 Dressing While Your Body Changes\n24:42 GLP-1s and Fashion\n29:00 Finding Freedom Through Style\n\nThe Weigh In is a Weight Watchers podcast and is not intended as medical advice. Talk to your doctor.\n\nProduced by @DearMediaStudio",
