        "title": "Hacked Hunger and the Role of GLP-1s",
        "description": "What happened to our food, our bodies, and our ability to stop eating — and who's responsible? Writer and journalist Johann Hari tracked down the scientists who discovered GLP-1, and traveled the world investigating the food system that was engineered to override our satiety signals. Here, Hari discusses his personal journey on a GLP-1—from losing food as a coping mechanism to embracing self-compassion in a world that says weight loss should involve punishment.\n\nGuest: Johann Hari\n\n0:00 Introduction\n0:58 Johann’s Body Story\n5:28 Weight, Health, and Denial\n8:40 Medical Stigma and Obesity\n10:58 Body Positivity vs. Health\n15:40 How Food Systems Changed\n17:58 Why We Don’t Feel Full\n18:38 How GLP-1s Work\n21:09 Why GLP-1s Feel Like Cheating\n23:57 Rethinking Weight and Willpower\n25:03 Learning Self-Compassion\n26:05 Men, Body Image, and GLP-1s\n29:00 Understanding GLP-1 Risks\n30:32 Losing Food as Comfort\n33:28 Grief, Health, and Hope\n\nThe Weigh In is a Weight Watchers podcast and is not intended as medical advice. Talk to your doctor.\n\nProduced by  ⁨@DearMediaStudio⁩",
