        "description": "Some things you only say to your best friend. This time, Susie Banikarim — Emmy-winning journalist, podcast host, and one of Samhita's closest friends — is saying them out loud.\n\nThe shame she has felt for being overweight, wanting to lose weight, and being on a GLP-1 (and still not being thin). How women privately support each other and share information about these medications. Intentional weight loss as a dirty word.\n\nAnd Susie's radical declaration: she doesn't care about being thin or what people think about her journey anymore.\n\nGuest: Susie Banikarim\n\n0:00 Introduction\n1:29 Growing Up With Body Shame\n4:59 Discovering GLP-1s\n6:27 Letting Go of Shame\n8:07 How GLP-1s Change Food Noise\n10:38 Is Taking GLP-1 Cheating?\n13:03 Health Over Thinness\n16:02 Rethinking Body Image\n21:46 Body Culture in Newsrooms\n23:44 Why GLP-1s Get Judged\n27:34 Intentional Weight Loss\n32:19 Changing Your Mind Publicly\n37:36 When Thin Isn’t The Goal\n\nThe Weigh In is a Weight Watchers podcast and is not intended as medical advice. Talk to your doctor.\n\nProduced by @DearMediaStudio",
